## <div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 10px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
<h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Learning to Manage a Club – Lesson # 3</h1>
<p style="margin: 0;"><i>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</i></p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 10th Grade (CEFR: B1.1)</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Let's Start a Club!</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Learning to Manage a Club</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Narrate a story or an experience in a structured way. Interactive: Negotiate project roles and tasks within a group.</p>
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can narrate a personal experience related to a club activity by including key details and a clear sequence of events (e.g., "Last year, I joined a sports club at school. First, I signed up during the club fair and then attended weekly practice sessions. During those meetings, I learned new skills and made new friends. Finally, we participated in a school tournament, and it was an unforgettable experience.").
Can negotiate project roles in a group discussion about starting a club by suggesting real club positions and responsibilities (e.g., "Let's decide who will be the president to lead meetings, the secretary to take notes, and the treasurer to manage the club's budget.").
Can express a preference for a club role and explain reasons (e.g., "I'd like to be the treasurer because I am good at math.").</p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <thead>
    <tr style="background-color: #e0e6ea; border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 17%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts by showing pictures of various school clubs (e.g., sports club, art club, debate club). Students, in pairs, discuss which club they would like to join and why. They practice asking "What type of club would you like to join?" and responding, "I'd like to join the ___ club because...". The teacher encourages them to use vocabulary like 'interests', 'activities', 'social', 'team-based'.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models narrating a personal experience: "Last year, I joined a book club. First, I signed up at the school fair. Then, we had weekly meetings where we discussed different books. It was a great experience, and I made new friends." The teacher also models the pronunciation of verbs ending in -ate (e.g., "delegate," "coordinate," "negotiate") and the contrastive sounds /pr/ and /tr/ in "project" and "treasure."</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did I join the club yesterday or last year?" (Checks understanding of simple past for narration).</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'I'd like to join,' am I talking about the past or the future?" (Checks understanding of expressing preferences).</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Let's Start a Club!")</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short audio dialogue between two high school students, Mariana and David, discussing their ideas for starting a new "Community Service Club." The dialogue features:
          <ul>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Simple present for preferences: "I like the idea of a club that helps the community." "There are many types of clubs, but this one feels important."</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Imperatives for instructions/suggestions: "Let's plan activities for the neighborhood clean-up." "First, set goals." "Then, assign roles."</li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Vocabulary: 'goals', 'members', 'responsibilities', 'roles', 'meetings', 'project', 'community', 'plan', 'organize', 'coordinate', 'assign', 'participate', 'supportive'.</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students will listen for specific details about club organization and the negotiation of initial ideas for a club, preparing them for interactive speaking about club management.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (oral responses required):</b></p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What kind of club do Mariana and David want to create?" (Students state the club type).</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False statements:</b> The teacher reads statements like: "Mariana thinks it's easy to manage a club." "They discuss specific roles like 'president' and 'secretary'." Students say "True" or "False" and briefly explain why.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Students verbally match club roles (e.g., 'President', 'Treasurer') to potential responsibilities mentioned (e.g., 'lead meetings', 'manage budget').</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Speaking)</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Speaking: expressing preferences using simple present; narrating past experiences using simple past; giving instructions/suggestions using imperatives. Using vocabulary related to club management and roles. Focusing on pronunciation of target sounds (/pr/, /tr/, /p/, /t/) and stress on -ate verbs and imperatives.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice: Sentence Expansion & Pronunciation:</b> The teacher provides sentence beginnings related to club experiences or preferences. Students verbally complete them and read them aloud.
            <ul style="list-style-type: circle; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Last year, I joined a ____ club, and I ____." (e.g., "Last year, I joined a *sports* club, and I *made* new friends.")</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I'd like to be the ____ because I am good at ____." (e.g., "I'd like to be the *treasurer* because I am good at math.")</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"To start a club, first, ____ goals, then ____ activities." (e.g., "To start a club, first, *set* goals, then *plan* activities.")</li>
            </ul>
            The teacher explicitly corrects pronunciation of sounds like /pr/ in "project" and /tr/ in "treasure," and stresses verbs like "delegate," "coordinate," "negotiate."</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice: Guided Dialogue:</b> In pairs, students receive dialogue prompts to discuss club preferences and past experiences.
            <ul style="list-style-type: circle; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student A: "What type of club would you like to *participate* in at school?"</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student B: "I'd like to join a ____ club because ____. Last year, I ____, and it was a ____ experience."</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student A: "That sounds interesting! How do you think we should *manage* a new club?"</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student B: "First, we should *create* a *structure*. Then, we need to *assign* *responsibilities*."</li>
            </ul>
            The teacher walks around, listening and providing immediate feedback on grammatical accuracy and pronunciation.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction / Peer Check:</b> Students turn to a new partner. Each student narrates a personal experience related to a club activity they were in (or wish they were in), including 2-3 key details and a sequence of events. The partner listens and provides feedback on clarity and use of target vocabulary (e.g., 'structured', 'organized', 'collaborative').</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 min</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Let's Start a Club!")</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Group Role-play & Negotiation. Students work in groups of 4-5.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Activity: "Our Dream Club Board Meeting"</b></p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group will imagine they are forming a new school club (e.g., a "Digital Arts Club," "Environmental Action Team," or "Cultural Exchange Group").</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Their task is to <b>negotiate project roles and tasks</b> within their group for this new club. They must decide who will be the president, secretary, treasurer, activity coordinator, or other relevant club positions.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students must express their preference for a role and explain their reasons, drawing on their skills or past experiences (e.g., "I'd like to be the treasurer because I am good at math and can *manage* the budget efficiently. Last year, I helped *organize* a fundraiser.").</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They should use imperatives to suggest actions and responsibilities (e.g., "Let's *plan* our first *event* by next month," "Make sure to *schedule* our *meetings* regularly").</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They must respond to *feedback* and *suggestions* from group members clearly and respectfully.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">After negotiation, each group briefly presents their club's name, main *goals*, and the assigned *roles* and primary *responsibilities* of each *member* to the class.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">12-15 min</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist and peer assessment.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group presents their negotiated club roles and a brief explanation of why each member was assigned their role (e.g., "Our president, [Name], will *lead meetings* and *coordinate* our *project* because she is very *organized*."). During the group work, the teacher circulates, making notes on a checklist.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Speaking):</b></p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible pronunciation:</b> Clear articulation of words, including correct stress on verbs ending in -ate (e.g., "delegate," "negotiate") and differentiation of /pr/ vs /tr/ sounds.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of target vocabulary:</b> Incorporates a range of vocabulary words (e.g., 'responsibilities', 'manage', 'coordinate', 'goal-oriented', 'inclusive') from the lesson.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity and coherence:</b> Explains preferences and narrates experiences clearly and in a structured way (e.g., using sequence markers like "first, then, finally").</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaborative negotiation:</b> Actively participates in group discussion, suggests roles, explains reasons, and responds to *feedback* and *suggestions* from peers.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar accuracy:</b> Uses simple present for descriptions/preferences, simple past for narration, and imperatives for instructions/suggestions accurately.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following prompts orally or in writing:</p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one new word or phrase you used today when talking about clubs?"</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How effectively did you *negotiate* your *role* in the group? What could you do better next time?"</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b></p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the most challenging part of narrating an experience or *negotiating* *roles* today, and how did you overcome it?"</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can the skills we practiced today help you in real-life *team* or *community* *projects*?"</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in promoting speaking skills and engagement? (e.g., specific activities, grouping strategies, teacher feedback).</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson to further support students' speaking fluency or accuracy, especially regarding pronunciation or specific grammar points?</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson focused on speaking about clubs and negotiating roles. In Lesson 4, students will use the discussed club structure and roles to write a formal club proposal, reinforcing the vocabulary and grammatical structures in a written context.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3-5 min</p>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>